## Phase 3 — Chunk Quality & Smart Sampling
*Fix the empty chunk problem and the holistic-document / niche-query mismatch.*

### 3.1 — Minimum Quality Filter (MODIFY `chunker.ts`)

**Problem solved:** Short, low-information chunks (page numbers, headers, table of contents lines, single-sentence footers) pollute the sample and skew quality scores downward.

**Add before any chunk is pushed to the array:**

```typescript
const MIN_CHUNK_WORDS = 20;      // Fewer than 20 words is almost never meaningful content
const MIN_CHUNK_CHARS = 100;     // Absolute floor
const TOC_PATTERN = /^(\d+\.?\s{1,5}.{3,60}\s+\d{1,4}\s*)+$/m; // "1. Introduction ... 12"
const HEADER_ONLY_PATTERN = /^[A-Z][A-Z\s]{0,40}$/;             // "CHAPTER THREE"
const PAGE_NUMBER_PATTERN = /^\s*\d{1,4}\s*$/;                   // Just a number

function isSubstantiveChunk(text: string): boolean {
  const trimmed = text.trim();
  if (trimmed.length < MIN_CHUNK_CHARS) return false;
  if (trimmed.split(/\s+/).length < MIN_CHUNK_WORDS) return false;
  if (TOC_PATTERN.test(trimmed)) return false;
  if (HEADER_ONLY_PATTERN.test(trimmed)) return false;
  if (PAGE_NUMBER_PATTERN.test(trimmed)) return false;
  return true;
}
```

**Log every filtered chunk** with the reason — this is what the user was asking for with the console log request.

