## Phase 4 — UX & Experience Layer
*The accuracy improvements from Phases 2–3 are worthless if users don't understand or trust the results.*

### 4.1 — Actionable Feedback Engine (MODIFY `aggregator.ts` + UI)

**Problem solved:** Users see a score and a decision with no idea what to do next.

**New `decide()` return type:**
```typescript
interface DecisionResult {
  decision: "proceed" | "confirm-with-user" | "block";
  headline: string;         // Short, plain English verdict
  reason: string;           // Why this decision was made
  nextSteps: NextStep[];    // NEW
}

interface NextStep {
  priority: "high" | "medium";
  action: string;           // One specific, concrete thing the user can do
}
```

**Decision → next step mapping:**

| Situation | Next Step shown |
|---|---|
| Blocked: intent mismatch | "Upload a document specifically about [domain from expanded intent]. You uploaded something about [detected topic]." |
| Blocked: poor scan quality | "Rescan at 300 DPI or higher. If scanning from a phone, ensure even lighting and no shadow across the text." |
| Blocked: too sparse | "This document may be a template or a summary. Upload the full, completed version." |
| Borderline: mixed quality | "The pages from [range] scored well. Consider extracting just those pages and re-uploading if the rest of the document isn't relevant." |
| Borderline: partial intent | "Your document covers [detected domain] broadly. Narrow your intent to match: try '[specific refined intent suggestion]'." |
| Proceed | "Your document is ready. [N] chunks will be passed to the dataset generator." |

**UI presentation:** Show next steps as a numbered action list below the score, not buried in a paragraph. Each step has an icon (🔄 rescan, 📄 re-export, ✏️ edit intent, etc.).

